rota lap 5186, row 1 -- Air-Saturn, the row that feels; law and boundary. Read foundations/20260826-021732_air-the-row-that-feels.md. Air presses a claimed boundary to feel whether the hand passes through, and the boundary under the hand this lap was the assert itself: a witness quoting a leg's name looked like a wall and turned out to be a substring test a sibling line walks straight through.
think Last lap built control_leg_heard, which counts legs no witness quotes. Its own header declared an upper bound it could not reach -- a witness quoting a name is credited with hearing it, whatever the assert says. Air asked what else that credit hides.
think Read generated_page_freshness: the witness asserts contains "debt_paid=yes" and the control emits both debt_paid and ledger_debt_paid. Rishi's contains is `find_word_op` over a raw substring (rishi/src/main.rye:1290), so the longer line satisfies the shorter assert. Proven in a two-line pen before anything was built.
think Tried the anchoring cure first and it does not exist here: a Rishi string literal carries no newline, and a backslash-n escape matched nothing against a real line start. So the cure is a NAME, and the reading ratchets rather than gating at zero.
think Counted distinct SHORT legs rather than sibling pairs, because two siblings over one leg is one hole and one rename closes both. Required the short name to be a leg the control actually emits: with no such leg there is nothing that can read no, and a diagnostic figure a witness quotes is a different question.
think Skipped generic-wall pairs, since a wall derives whole `=no` LINES and no substring reaches it. Proven in the pen rather than assumed.
obs My own five new legs masked five elder ones on the first draft -- mask_ceiling_bites_one_past ends ceiling_bites_one_past -- so the instrument counted itself before it counted anybody. Renamed to mask_bound_* on the same touch, which is the cure read from the inside.
obs The mutation that carries the most weight is the character class before the name. comm hands the sibling search a name the control emits, so a bare `<name>$` matches that very line and every leg masks itself.
obs Closed generated_page_freshness on touch and it paid both readings at once -- the two maskers were themselves unheard, so renaming them and naming them took unheard 35 to 33 and masked 16 to 14.
obs Two fleet-wide reds surfaced in the hot pass. fold_shelf_link_repoint read fold_depth_lost=2 and both were my own lane's shelves carrying a link at the card's depth rather than the shelf's; the repointer applied the one correction each resolves under, GREEN. itinerary_list read broken_runs=1 on a line of a peer's account opening `32. Warm floor`, which its reader took for item 32 of a run starting at 1 -- I reflowed the line, then the rebase brought 01a7bdc31, which repairs the reader instead, so I dropped the reflow and left the peer's paragraph byte for byte. A guard misreading prose is the reader's red, and its owner had it.
